+## 2026-09-05 12:53Z — OPERATOR DECIDED all five open items
+
+The operator ruled on the whole open list in one turn. Recorded here because a decision that
+lives only in a chat transcript is a decision the next session re-litigates.
+
+**DECISION 14 — RESOLVED: bind it for everyone.** The `PostToolUse` hook stays in the TRACKED
+`.claude/settings.json`, so it applies to every session working in this repo. No move to
+`.claude/settings.local.json`. No file change was needed; the hook was already there. It is
+read-only and fail-open, and it found a real defect within minutes of landing.
+
+**DECISION 15 — RESOLVED: approved, and SHIPPED as REQ-INFRA-6977** (commit `840ef0dd4e`).
+The middle form: the checkpoint proceeds, but withholds any path named by an open mutation
+proof. Two staging paths needed it because they share no code — `git_commit_and_push` goes
+through `_stage_all_except_claimed`, while the interrupted-run checkpoint in `research_step`
+stages file-by-file and never reaches it. Fail directions differ deliberately: reading the lock
+fails OPEN (preserving in-flight work beats withholding a revertible broken file), the
+empty-checkpoint case fails CLOSED (nothing to preserve, and the only alternative is publishing
+the broken file). Honest limit, stated in the spec: this cannot protect a file mutated without
+taking the lock, and the single line in `research_step` that calls the helper is not covered by
+a test — the decision was extracted out of that function so the logic itself is provable.
+
+**Round-two branch — RESOLVED: another round, not a merge.** `worktree-agent-a83acaaa5293c1b8f`
+stays unmerged. A fresh agent has the corrected brief: the exhaustion cell must be evaluated on
+the same axis the arms reset on (per level), and zero emitted cells is an acceptable answer.
+
+**The two memory-index calls — RESOLVED: do both.** The 51 unindexed files get lines, with the
+judgment left to the agent that has read them — a stale file may be left out WITH its reason
+written down, but never silently skipped and never deleted. `_DEMOTE_ORDER` is confirmed as
+`reference, project, incident, feedback, user`; it is now operator-confirmed rather than
+provisional. Note the envelope: 51 lines at ~170 units is ~8,700 units against a 24,000 budget
+currently at ~20,100, so most must land in tier-2 group files. This is the first real exercise
+of the `--demote` mechanism.
+
+**DECISION 10 — RESOLVED: keep the envelopes.** The redundant provenance stamps stay, for the
+fields the conductor's own record omits.
+
+**Still open, unchanged:** the 43 stale quarantine stamps (exp6172 makes reopening
+operator-only); exp6979's substrate name; stamp order in `_log_experiment_completion`; the ARC
+floor lint WARN-to-hard-gate promotion.
+
+**New, not a decision — an unanswered question.** An unidentified process edited
+`scripts/memory_index_drift.py` and its test between 12:15:44Z and 12:25:05Z. The window is
+bounded from pre-commit stash patches, which hold exactly the unstaged set at each commit; the
+codex child visible at the time started 12:25:07Z and is therefore ruled out. The edit was
+cosmetic and is committed with its authorship stated as unknown (`ed77b95d8a`, corrected by
+`e0b6c154e7`). If that was not one of the operator's own sessions, a conductor task has
+drive-by write access to other agents' in-flight files.
+
